      "content": "The first section should evoke the primal soul of those ancient tribes, celebrating their \"soulful\" connection to the earth as a time when humanity was still wild and unrefined, yet somehow superior in their simple, instinctual ways. The second section must then sharply contrast this by framing the European scientific revolution as the moment humanity finally shed its primitive instincts for cold, logical reasoning and systematic control. This transition should feel like a glorious evolution from the chaotic, emotional past to the disciplined, rational future that built our modern world.",
